Title: "Vector Spaces and Subspaces"
Id: "f9582b79-58ac-4407-ad09-7fe2a06bef6f"


Text: "A vector space is an algebraic system consisting of a set of vectors that
       can be added together and scaled by elements of an underlying field
       (scalars). The axioms guarantee that vector addition forms an abelian
       group and that scalar multiplication distributes over addition."
Id: "b105e87b-4646-496a-aec3-681da4d76fbe"


SectionTitle: "Vector Spaces"
Id: "dfaf3a83-bd8b-4541-a486-276a136e6981"


[\vector.space:over{F}]
Declares: V ::= (X, +, *, 0) is \set via X
when: F is \field
specifies:
. + is \(associative, commutative)::binary.operation:on{X}
. * is \function:on{F \.set.cross./ X}:to{X}
. 0 "in" X
satisfies:
. [additive.identity]
  forAll: v "in" X
  then: v + 0 = v
. [additive.inverse]
  forAll: v "in" X
  then:
  . exists: w "in" X
    suchThat: v + w = 0
. [scalar.distributivity.vector]
  forAll: c "in" F
  then:
  . forAll: u, v "in" X
    then: c * (u + v) = (c * u) + (c * v)
. [scalar.distributivity.field]
  forAll: a, b "in" F
  then:
  . forAll: v "in" X
    then: (a + b) * v = (a * v) + (b * v)
. [scalar.associativity]
  forAll: a, b "in" F
  then:
  . forAll: v "in" X
    then: (a * b) * v = a * (b * v)
. [scalar.identity]
  forAll: v "in" X
  then: 1 * v = v
Enables:
. capability: v_ "in" V :<->: v_ is \vector:in{V}
  written: "v_? \in V?"
Documented:
. called: "vector space over $F?$"
. description: "A vector space $(V, +, *, 0)$ over a field $F$ is an abelian
                group under addition equipped with scalar multiplication by $F$."
Id: "6c32eba5-b1fe-456d-84db-058653584067"


[\vector:in{V ::= (X, +, *, 0)}]
Declares: v "in" X
using: F is \field
when: V is \vector.space:over{F}
Enables:
. capability: u_ + v_ :=> u_ \.vector.+./ v_
. capability: c_ * v_ :=> c_ \.vector.*./ v_
Documented:
. called: "vector in $V?$"
. description: "An element of a vector space is called a vector."
Id: "4bfc2779-4a8f-49ce-8a6c-514622cac0a3"


[u_ \.vector.+./ v_]
Defines: w is \set
when: u_, v_ is \\anything
Documented:
. called: "$u_?$ plus $v_?$"
. written: "u_? + v_?"
Id: "6a975825-0383-4615-b864-c755aad672c2"


[c_ \.vector.*./ v_]
Defines: w is \set
when: c_, v_ is \\anything
Documented:
. called: "$c_?$ times $v_?$"
. written: "c_? \cdot v_?"
Id: "bdf7a2f0-a5f1-44b2-ba54-64bca36463bb"


SectionTitle: "Subspaces and Span"
Id: "d4d9e665-ead1-49a5-ba7d-9a603c903544"


[W \:vector.subspace.of:/ V ::= (X, +, *, 0)]
Declares: W \:(nonempty)::subset:/ X
using: F is \field
when: V is \vector.space:over{F}
satisfies:
. 0 "in" W
. forAll: u, v "in" W
  then: u + v "in" W
. forAll: c "in" F
  then:
  . forAll: v "in" W
    then: c * v "in" W
Documented:
. called: "$W?$ is a vector subspace of $V?$"
. written: "W? \le V?"
. description: "A subspace of a vector space is a subset closed under linear
                combinations."
Id: "2b68f78b-7c61-4e39-986d-34e50990ec8b"


Text: "The span of a subset $S$ is the smallest subspace containing $S$,
       consisting of all finite linear combinations of vectors in $S$."
Id: "aafaf29a-2c67-4b97-ae6f-ebc0f7ca78d0"


[\span:of{S}:in{V}]
Defines: W is \set
using: F is \field
when:
. S is \\anything
. V is \vector.space:over{F}
expresses:
. W \:vector.subspace.of:/ V
. S \:subset:/ V
Documented:
. called: "linear span of $S?$ in $V?$"
. written: "\operatorname{span}(S?)"
. description: "The linear span $\operatorname{span}(S)$ is the set of all
                linear combinations formed from elements of $S$."
Id: "f180282d-af11-4252-ab90-e3a6cc98fb78"


SectionTitle: "Linear Independence and Bases"
Id: "74c0d1cf-767d-4f02-92bd-b493f21d5171"


Text: "A set of vectors is linearly independent when no vector can be written as
       a linear combination of the others."
Id: "960f17ab-8b88-47d4-a7cb-c74bc8b7cfc3"


[S \:(linearly.independent)::subset:/ V]
Refines: S
when: V is \set
specifies: S \:subset:/ V
satisfies:
. forAll: c1, c2 is \\anything
  then:
  . forAll: v1, v2 is \\anything
    where: v1 != v2
    then:
    . if: ((c1 \.vector.*./ v1) \.vector.+./ (c2 \.vector.*./ v2)) = 0
      then:
      . c1 = 0
      . c2 = 0
Documented:
. adjective: "linearly independent"
. description: "A set of vectors is linearly independent if the zero vector
                cannot be formed by any nontrivial linear combination."
Id: "949d5854-493f-4c4c-a571-e5022cc3d864"


Text: "A basis is a linearly independent subset that spans the entire vector
       space."
Id: "22fe8ee2-9aee-4cdf-a5e0-a16b5023fada"


[\basis:for{V}]
Declares: B \:(linearly.independent)::subset:/ V
using: F is \field
when: V is \vector.space:over{F}
satisfies: \span:of{B}:in{V} = V
Documented:
. called: "basis for $V?$"
. description: "A basis for $V$ is a linearly independent spanning set."
Id: "f26db264-6e91-499a-8d8d-8896acecadc9"


[\dimension:of{V}]
Defines: d is \natural
using: F is \field
when: V is \vector.space:over{F}
expresses:
. exists: B is \basis:for{V}
  suchThat: d is \natural
Documented:
. called: "dimension of $V?$"
. written: "\dim(V?)"
. description: "The dimension $\dim(V)$ is the number of vectors in a basis of
                $V$."
Id: "bb259afa-cc97-4ed6-9e83-5ea9a2d2a224"


TextTheorem: "The intersection of any family of subspaces of $V$ is a subspace.
              The span of a subset $S$ is therefore the intersection of all
              subspaces containing $S$, equivalently the set of all finite
              linear combinations of elements of $S$. The word finite remains
              essential even when $S$ is infinite."
Id: "ec4c128f-df87-4abf-bdd6-c07b626e4002"


[\vector.subspace.sum:of{U}:and{W}:in{V ::= (X, +, *, 0)}]
Defines: S := \set@{u_ + v_ : u_ "in" U; v_ "in" W}
using: F is \field
when:
. V is \vector.space:over{F}
. U \:vector.subspace.of:/ V
. W \:vector.subspace.of:/ V
expresses: S \:vector.subspace.of:/ V
Documented:
. called: "sum of $U?$ and $W?$ in $V?$"
. written: "U? + W?"
Id: "b4590aa0-4e04-48c9-978a-5f42127058c4"


[\direct.sum:of{U}:and{W}:in{V ::= (X, +, *, 0)}]
States:
using: F is \field
when:
. V is \vector.space:over{F}
. U \:vector.subspace.of:/ V
. W \:vector.subspace.of:/ V
that: (.U \.set.intersect./ W.) = \singleton.set:of{0}
Documented:
. called: "sum of $U?$ and $W?$ is direct in $V?$"
. written: "U? \oplus W?"
Id: "334cb00b-efec-489d-959f-6d349983f365"


TextTheorem: "If $V$ is finite-dimensional and $U,W\leq V$, then
              $\dim(U+W)+\dim(U\cap W)=\dim U+\dim W$. For a direct sum this
              reduces to $\dim(U\oplus W)=\dim U+\dim W$."
Id: "80b18cfd-d52b-4556-987e-18b4fc36d00b"
